# liblouis: Unified English Braille Code New Zealand (Grade 1)
#
#-index-name: English, unified, New Zealand, uncontracted
#-display-name: Unified English uncontracted braille as used in New Zealand
#+language:en
#+region:*-NZ
#+type:literary
#+contraction:no
#+grade:1
#+system:ueb-nz
#
# This table implements the policy of the Braille Authority of New
# Zealand Aotearoa Trust, that vowel macrons be indicated in braille
# by the single cell prefix dots 456 (see
# https://www.banzat.org.nz/documents/BANZATPolicy8TranscribingMaoriTextInBraille.docx
# ). Although under this policy this should only apply to words in the
# Māori language, the reality is that many Māori words are commonly
# used in English texts without being marked up as Māori. This table
# is provided so readers reading in the English language can have such
# words presented in braille using the same dots 4-5-6 prefix to
# indicate macrons.
#
#  This file is part of liblouis.
#
#  liblouis is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify it
#  under the terms of the GNU Lesser General Public License as
